el architecture/workflow figure for a biomedical multi-modal foundation model. Panel (a) “Overall Architecture” shows inputs from whole slide images, omics, and pathology reports processed by modality-specific tokenizers/encoders, sequence projectors, a Universal Sequence Transformer, and task-specific projection heads. Panel (b) “Stage 1: Pre-training Universal Sequence Transformer” shows contrastive and masked language modeling objectives across WSI, omics, and text features, including inter-modal, inter-sample, and intra-modal contrast. Panel (c) “Stage 2: Training Task Projection Heads with Downstream Tasks” shows downstream applications including cancer subtyping, survival analysis, and report generation. No quantitative axes or experimental results are shown; the main content is a proposed multimodal training pipeline/architecture.\",\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:1375:        \"page_no\": 4,\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:1376:        \"selection_score\": 267,\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:1377:        \"selection_reasons\": [\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:1378:          \"1 model-name tokens match\",\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:1379:          \"architecture/workflow figure\",\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:1380:          \"model name appears in figure text\",\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:1381:          \"route cites this figure number\"\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:1382:        ],\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:1383:        \"sha256\": \"1082c05fd353b8d9f16bb5a81f5d19d7729869a16478cd9438a685c9dc40dd10\"\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:1384:      },\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:1385:      \"routes\": [\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:1386:        {\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:1387:          \"route_id\": \"route_dcf0