rom LLM-BFT. a : LLM-BFT generates profile texts for entities of interest (e.g., a specific gene). The gene profile text is encoded by OpenAI TEXT-EMBEDDING-ADA-002 (the same text encoder GenePT uses) to obtain gene embeddings, so that GenePT (GPT-4o + ada-002) and LLM-BFT (BFT-70B + ada-002) differ only in the LLM that produces the profile text. b : For a single-cell dataset, gene embeddings are weighted by gene expression values to generate cell embeddings.\",\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:1929:        \"description\": \"SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\\n\\nWorkflow/model architecture schematic with two labeled panels, **a** and **b**. Panel **a** shows an LLM-based gene text embedding pipeline: a user prompt (“Tell me about gene.”) is processed by **LLM-BFT**, producing an LLM response with gene name/function/interaction text; texts for gene x through gene y are converted via **Text to embedding** into a **gene embedding (N, 2048)** matrix. Panel **b** shows a cell-by-gene expression matrix for **M cells** and **N genes** multiplied by the **gene embedding (N, 2048)** matrix to produce a **cell embedding (M, 2048)** matrix. Main visible message: gene-level text embeddings are derived from LLM responses and combined with gene expression data to generate cell embeddings.\",\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:1930:        \"page_no\": 17,\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:1931:        \"selection_score\": 73,\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:1932:        \"selection_reasons\": [\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:1933:          \"2 model-name tokens match\",\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:1934:          \"architecture/workflow figure\",\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:1935:          \"route cites this figure number\"\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:1936:        ],\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:1937:        \"sha256\": \"67fe2b141b93b