t-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:2068:      ],\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:2069:      \"fusion_topologies\": [\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:2070:        \"cross_attention\",\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:2071:        \"tokenizer_sequence\"\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:2072:      ],\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:2073:      \"text_roles\": [\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:2074:        \"instruction_or_query\"\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:2075:      ],\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:2076:      \"figure\": {\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:2077:        \"asset\": \"assets/figures/june_update_2026_06_10_rec_000194_figure_001.png\",\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:2078:        \"source_path\": \"data/docling_include_vlm_52_2026-07-10_nolimits/figures/june_update_2026_06_10_rec_000194/figure_001.png\",\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:2079:        \"figure_index\": 1,\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:2080:        \"caption\": \"Figure 1: (a) Embeddings (E) from Biological Foundation Models (BioFMs) are input to Bio-BLIP to provide multiple modalities of information, here from AlphaGenome , GenePT , and ESM-2 . (b) Modality-specific Q-formers align diverse biological embeddings with captions of genomic variants, which contain functional and locational information. The Q-formers output query tokens encoding relevant information from each modality. (c) The Master Qformer integrates modality-specific tokens through cross-attention, producing a fixed-length visual prefix (d) The LLM, its weights frozen , takes as input the multimodal prefix and a prompt. During pretraining, the LLM loss backpropagates only to train the Q-formers. Pretraining and evaluation is conducted on variant annotation; all weights are frozen and the model is then applied to downstream evaluation tasks.\",\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:2081:        \"description\": \"SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\\n\\nModel architecture/workflow diagram labeled “BioBLIP Architecture.” It shows panel-like labels A-D: A indicates multiple input embedding sources (AlphaGenome Ref/Alt embeddings, GenoPT embeddings, ESM Protein embeddings) as blue triangular inputs E1, E2, … En; B shows modality-specific query modules (“DNA Qformer,” “Gene Qformer,” “Protein Qformer”) producing DNA/gene/protein-specific query tokens; C shows a “Master Qformer” receiving query tokens plus an instruction describing genomic variant context and outputting a fixed-length variant prefix; D shows this prefix fed with a text prompt into a “Frozen LLM,” producing a generated variant annotation JSON.\\n\\nNo quantitative axes or plots are present. The biological/model content shown is a multimodal genomic variant annotation architecture integrating DNA, gene, and protein embeddings for tasks including variant annotation, target gene identification, and regulatory variant prioritization. Main visible finding/claim: BioBLIP uses chained Q-former modules to convert heterogeneous biological embeddings into an LLM-compatible prefix for structured variant annotation.\",\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:2082:        \"page_no\": 2,\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:2083:        \"selection_score\": 293,\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:2084:        \"selection_reasons\": [\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:2085:          \"2 model-name tokens match\",\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:2086:          \"architecture/workflow figure\",\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:2087:          \"model name appears in figure text\",\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:2088:          \"route cites this figure number\"\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:2089:        ],\ndocs/input-representa