_rec_003214/figure_002.png\",\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:2549:        \"figure_index\": 2,\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:2550:        \"caption\": \"Figure 2: The overview of BioMedGPT-10B. BioMedGPT-LM is the large language model of BioMedGPT, which serves as a cognitive core to jointly comprehend various biological modalities through natural language. In BioMedGPT-10B, the parameter size of the large language model is 7B. BioMedGPT-10B adopts GraphMVP [Liu et al., 2022] as the 2D molecular graph encoder, ESM2-3B [Lin et al., 2022] as the protein sequence encoder, and conducts feature space alignment via a neural network adaptor. BioMedGPT can be applied to many multimodal downstream tasks such as biomedical QA, molecule QA, and protein QA.\",\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:2551:        \"description\": \"SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\\n\\nFigure type: multi-panel workflow/model architecture schematic for BioMedGPT.\\n\\nVisible panels and labels:\\n- Top panel: “BioMedGPT-LM: Incremental Training on Biomedical Corpus,” showing Meta AI LLaMA 2 trained on biomedical corpora including arXiv, PubMed Central, and WIPO, producing “BioMedGPT-LM.”\\n- Bottom-left panel: “BioMedGPT-10B: Multi-Modal Alignment between Biomedical and Natural Language,” showing molecule and protein encoders aligned with BioMedGPT-LM using instruction/question inputs.\\n- Right panel: “Downstream Tasks,” showing example Biomedical QA, Molecule QA, and Protein QA prompts with answer boxes.\\n\\nAxes/legend: no plot axes or quantitative legend are present.\\n\\nBiological/model quantity shown: model training and multimodal alignment pipeline connecting biomedical text, molecular structures, and protein structures to question-answering tasks.\\n\\nMain visible finding/message: the figure presents BioMedGPT as a LLaMA 2-derived biomedical language model further aligned with molecule and protein encoders for biomedical, molecular, and protein QA tasks.\