n:30455:        \"biological_payload\",\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:30456:        \"instruction_or_query\"\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:30457:      ],\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:30458:      \"figure\": {\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:30459:        \"asset\": \"assets/figures/full_2026_07_06_rec_001889_figure_001.png\",\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:30460:        \"source_path\": \"data/docling_include_vlm_52_2026-07-10_nolimits/figures/full_2026_07_06_rec_001889/figure_001.png\",\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:30461:        \"figure_index\": 1,\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:30462:        \"caption\": \"\",\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:30463:        \"description\": \"SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\\n\\nMulti-panel scientific figure showing a multimodal single-cell foundation model overview and dataset/task summaries.\\n\\nPanel a is a concentric donut/ring chart summarizing dataset coverage by modality, species, age group, brain region, and disease, with legends for categories such as epigenomics, transcriptomics, spatial transcriptomics; mouse, marmoset, macaque, human; prenatal to aged; cortical and other brain regions; and disease/normal classes.\\n\\nPanel b contains word-cloud summaries for metadata fields labeled Question Type, Class, Subclass, Region, Age group, and Disease, highlighting terms such as GABA, GL, oligo, Astro, region names, age values, Alzheimer, Normal, disease, and glioma.\\n\\nPanel c is a model/workflow architecture diagram. Cell and feature inputs from multi-omics and multi-species data are tokenized, passed through a gene encoder, projected with graph convolutional networks and cross-attention, then connected to a large language model with text input/output. Six example task panels are shown: cell type annotation, cell origin prediction, aging clock, disease status inference, gene mask prediction, and spatial mask prediction.\\n\\nPanel d shows a two-stage training strategy: Stage 1 freezes the gene encoder and LLM while training the projector; Stage 2 trains the gene encoder, projector, and LLM with LoRA.\\n\\nMain visible finding: the figure presents a unified architecture and training workflow for connecting single-cell/multi-omics biological features to LLM-based question answering across annotation, species/origin, aging, disease, and masked prediction tasks.\",\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:30464:        \"page_no\": 40,\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:30465:        \"selection_score\": 188,\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:30466:        \"selection_reasons\": [\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:30467:          \"architecture/workflow figure\",\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:30468:          \"route cites this figure number\"\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:30469:        ],\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:30470:        \"sha256\": \"61d87821f3e8330cd88afb7e918f6bd337957e7822931f73ad3c2fad8d4052ea\"\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:30471:      },\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:30472:      \"routes\": [\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:30473:        {\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:30474:          \"route_id\": \"route_072c223f12e5\",\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:30475:          \"configuration_id\": \"config_aa157476b0d5\",\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:30476:          \"route_label\": \"snRNA-seq gene expression to scMOBA\",\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:30477:          \"lifecycle_phase\": \"pretraining\",\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:30478:          \"task_or_configuration_verbatim\": \"feature-question-answer framework\",\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:30479:          \"s