   \"figure\": {\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:32267:        \"asset\": \"assets/figures/full_2026_07_06_rec_000063_figure_001.png\",\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:32268:        \"source_path\": \"data/docling_include_vlm_52_2026-07-10_nolimits/figures/full_2026_07_06_rec_000063/figure_001.png\",\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:32269:        \"figure_index\": 1,\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:32270:        \"caption\": \"Figure 1: Overview of the TISSUENARRATOR framework. A. TISSUENARRATOR takes as input a tissue patch, encodes individual cells into cell sentences, and assembles a spatial sentence from neighboring cells. The spatial sentence can be interpreted by an LLM with biological prior knowledge and contextual understanding to predict gene expressions in a cell and to answer questions about tissues. Text output of the LLM can be further transformed into gene expression levels. B. TISSUENARRATOR supports four downstream tasks: cell generation, neighborhood perturbation, genetic perturbation, and conversational tissue querying. For cell generation tasks, model-generated cell sentences can be converted back into gene expression space.\",\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:32271:        \"description\": \"SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\\n\\nWorkflow/model schematic with two labeled panels, **A** and **B**. Panel A shows a tissue patch converted into “cell sentences” with ordered gene lists, then into a “spatial sentence” containing ordered cells with position, metadata, cell type, and gene list. An LLM with biological prior knowledge/contextual understanding is used for generative prediction, including cell prediction and text prediction, and quantitative prediction of gene expression values for genes such as G1, G2, G3. Panel B lists applications: cell generation, conversational tissue querying, genetic perturbation, and neighborhood perturbation. No numerical experimental data or axes are shown; the main content is a conceptual architecture/workflow for spatial tissue modeling with language-model-style representations.\",\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:32272:        \"page_no\": 3,\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:32273:        \"selection_score\": 282,\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:32274:        \"selection_reasons\": [\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:32275:          \"1 model-name tokens match\",\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:32276:          \"architecture/workflow figure\",\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:32277:          \"model name appears in figure text\",\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:32278:          \"route cites this figure number\"\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:32279:        ],\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:32280:        \"sha256\": \"0befdb410abb4e546974eadd4f1986311baf5682f0c870a9c16a86bb69266aa4\"\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:32281:      },\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:32282:      \"routes\": [\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:32283:        {\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:32284:          \"route_id\": \"route_20d8a9154583\",\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:32285:          \"configuration_id\": \"config_30d5b1c1447b\",\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:32286:          \"route_label\": \"Spatial sentence fine-tuning\",\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:32287:          \"lifecycle_phase\": \"fine_tuning\",\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:32288:          \"task_or_configuration_verbatim\": \"next-token prediction\",\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:32289:          \"source_object_verbatim\": \"a tissue section\",\ndocs/input-representation-atlas/data/atlas.json:32290:          \"source_object_normalized\": \"tissue section\",\ndo